      "defect": "overstrong-title-or-statement",
      "evidence": "The title asserts \"Trivial action on the standard meridians fixes the punctures and the stem arcs up to isotopy\". The Statement instead concludes \"h(s_i) is homotopic to s_i relative to endpoints\" and declares that no choice principle is used. Proof 4.1 explicitly says: \"The intermediate paths need not be embeddings; upgrading this homotopy to an isotopy is a separate proper-arc result.\" That separate scoped proper-arc lemma assumes AC. Thus this item's proof establishes compact endpoint homotopy, not the isotopy advertised by its title.",
